ge_header$685be352-9a1d-4aca-9374-66032117e119","page_header",{"variation":53,"version":26,"items":54,"primary":56,"id":78,"slice_type":79,"slice_label":30},"cardWithImageNoCta",[55],{},{"CardImage":57,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":67,"CardText":68,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":58,"alt":61,"copyright":30,"url":62,"id":63,"edit":64},{"width":59,"height":60},1000,667,"A customer is crouched on the floor of their apartment, placing a cardboard parcel inside waterproof packaging.","how-to-package-books.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6XshZbqstJ9-We1_EVRI_LOCATION_04_5283.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6XshZbqstJ9-We1",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"transparent","none","How to wrap books for delivery",[69,72,75],{"type":34,"text":70,"spans":71},"Anyone who regularly sells items online knows you have to be careful when it comes to packing your parcels properly for shipping, especially when it comes to books.",[],{"type":34,"text":73,"spans":74},"Books might be sturdy, but they can still get damaged in transit. Poor packaging choices, lack of padding, and exposure to moisture can leave even the toughest books a little worse for wear.",[],{"type":34,"text":76,"spans":77},"To prevent this from happening, and to help you post your books securely, we’ve listed the best ways to package books.",[],"card$b41a97c6-75d3-4c57-a905-ee478866d9fe","card",{"variation":81,"version":26,"items":82,"primary":84,"id":99,"slice_type":100,"slice_label":30},"default-slice",[83],{},{"title":85,"bodyText":86,"isEco":21,"PaddingTop":21,"PaddingBottom":90,"NoMarginBottom":21,"hasButton":21,"buttonText":30,"buttonLink":91,"image":93},"How to package individual books",[87],{"type":34,"text":88,"spans":89},"For anyone packaging books for the first time, the following steps are key areas to consider when wrapping up an individual book for transport:",[],true,{"link_type":92},"Any",{"dimensions":94,"alt":95,"copyright":30,"url":96,"id":97,"edit":98},{"width":59,"height":60},"Customer sat at a desk holding two parcels that have been packaged and labelled, glancing down at them.","how-to-package-books.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6R6N5bqstJ9-SUJ_EVRI_LOCATION_05_8676.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6R6N5bqstJ9-SUJ",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"feature_banner$4a4d3430-108a-42a5-b8b9-cdd9fecbbc0c","feature_banner",{"variation":81,"version":26,"items":102,"primary":143,"id":146,"slice_type":147,"slice_label":30},[103,111,119,127,135],{"title":104,"content":105,"isNumbered":90,"icon":109,"image":110},"Pick a box with an extra inch or two of room",[106],{"type":34,"text":107,"spans":108},"This gives you additional room to slide in more padding for your book.",[],{},{},{"title":112,"content":113,"isNumbered":90,"icon":117,"image":118},"Carefully wrap your book in bubble wrap",[114],{"type":34,"text":115,"spans":116},"This ensures it’s fully covered in padding. Remember, you want this padding to be firm, but not so tight that it bends the book.",[],{},{},{"title":120,"content":121,"isNumbered":90,"icon":125,"image":126},"Secure your wrapping with tape",[122],{"type":34,"text":123,"spans":124},"Secure your bubble wrap with tape and then add a second layer for further protection.",[],{},{},{"title":128,"content":129,"isNumbered":90,"icon":133,"image":134},"Delicately slide your book into its packaging and stuff the gaps around it",[130],{"type":34,"text":131,"spans":132},"Using more bubble wrap or old newspaper, fill in any gaps to protect the book and prevent it from moving around.",[],{},{},{"title":136,"content":137,"isNumbered":90,"icon":141,"image":142},"Seal your package with packing tape",[138],{"type":34,"text":139,"spans":140},"Tap the top and bottom of your box and make sure any gaps are covered.",[],{},{},{"theme":30,"title":144,"description":145,"showPaddingTop":21},"Wrap your books in sturdy packaging","While you can use a toughened envelope lined with bubble wrap inside to send your books, it’s better to use a small box. A box is always the safest option when posting books. Just remember, a small box needs to be measured to match your book’s size.\n\nTo choose the best packaging, follow our steps below:","list_block$648e4197-96f7-4bb4-a939-7e26cba6c7b0","list_block",{"variation":53,"version":26,"items":149,"primary":151,"id":206,"slice_type":79,"slice_label":30},[150],{},{"CardImage":152,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":158,"CardText":159,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":153,"alt":154,"copyright":30,"url":155,"id":156,"edit":157},{"width":59,"height":60},"Customer carrying multiple parcels inside a ParcelShop store, ready to drop off for delivery","how-to-package-books.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6R1D5bqstJ9-SOx_EVRI_LOCATION_03_2468.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6R1D5bqstJ9-SOx",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"How to send multiple books",[160,164,177,183,188,193,198,203],{"type":34,"text":161,"spans":162,"direction":163},"Even the most experienced book sender will need to send multiple books together at some stage, especially if you plan to send several of them to a buyer in one go.",[],"ltr",{"type":34,"text":165,"spans":166,"direction":163},"Fortunately, if you're selling books online, then the process of packing multiple books is the same as posting a single book, there are just a few extra steps you’ll need to consider:",[167,175],{"start":168,"end":169,"type":170,"data":171},23,43,"hyperlink",{"link_type":172,"url":173,"target":174},"Web","how-to-package-books.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fguides\u002Fhow-to-sell-books-online","_self",{"start":168,"end":169,"type":176},"strong",{"type":178,"text":179,"spans":180,"direction":163},"o-list-item","Choose a box that’s big enough to house the number of books you want to send - make sure you have at least an inch or two of space around the edge for additional padding.",[181],{"start":45,"end":182,"type":176},76,{"type":178,"text":184,"spans":185,"direction":163},"Cushion the base of your box with bubble wrap – this will pad your box out and make ensure the base of your books are protected. ",[186],{"start":45,"end":187,"type":176},46,{"type":178,"text":189,"spans":190,"direction":163},"Wrap each book individually in bubble wrap – using the method mentioned above, carefully wrap all your books before stacking them on top of each other to make the most of your box’s space.",[191],{"start":45,"end":192,"type":176},42,{"type":178,"text":194,"spans":195,"direction":163},"Fill the boxes edges and gaps - taking more bubble wrap of old newspaper, fill in any gaps between your books and the box's edge, being sure to pad their top as well.",[196],{"start":45,"end":197,"type":176},29,{"type":178,"text":199,"spans":200,"direction":163},"Secure your box with packing tape – take your packaging tape and secure the base, lid, and box corners to make your box as sturdy as possible.",[201],{"start":45,"end":202,"type":176},33,{"type":34,"text":204,"spans":205,"direction":163},"The best way to pack books is to add enough padding for protection. Bubble wrap is exceedingly light, too, so it won’t impact the cost of postage!",[],"card$7c607924-49de-4591-9f71-2fda538cb481",{"variation":53,"version":26,"items":208,"primary":210,"id":236,"slice_type":79,"slice_label":30},[209],{},{"CardImage":211,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":216,"CardText":217,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":212,"alt":61,"copyright":30,"url":213,"id":214,"edit":215},{"width":59,"height":60},"how-to-package-books.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6XscpbqstJ9-We0_EVRI_LOCATION_04_5276.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6XscpbqstJ9-We0",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"How to package rare books",[218,221,227,231],{"type":34,"text":219,"spans":220},"If you want to send an antique or uncommon book to an expert or collector, you’ll need to package them securely to prevent damage. The steps we’ve already mentioned will help protect your older books from most damage, but to be extra safe, we’d recommend:",[],{"type":222,"text":223,"spans":224},"list-item","Wrapping books in an extra third\u002Ffourth layer of bubble wrap – this adds an extra layer of cushioning, which is great for a fragile or hardback books.",[225],{"start":45,"end":226,"type":176},60,{"type":222,"text":228,"spans":229},"Place cardboard dividers between each book – this keeps the book(s) in place, and prevents movement. ",[230],{"start":45,"end":169,"type":176},{"type":222,"text":232,"spans":233},"Put your wrapped book in a sealable plastic bag - to prevent any potential damp seeping inside.",[234],{"start":45,"end":235,"type":176},47,"card$46a6e9e4-c745-4132-94c4-18c2bae9b794",{"variation":81,"version":26,"items":238,"primary":240,"id":253,"slice_type":100,"slice_label":30},[239],{},{"title":241,"bodyText":242,"isEco":21,"PaddingTop":21,"PaddingBottom":90,"NoMarginBottom":21,"hasButton":21,"buttonText":30,"buttonLink":246,"image":247},"How to ship books",[243],{"type":34,"text":244,"spans":245},"Now that you’ve got your books packed, weighed, and ready to go, let's look at how to ship books correctly.",[],{"link_type":92},{"dimensions":248,"alt":249,"copyright":30,"url":250,"id":251,"edit":252},{"width":59,"height":60},"A courier scanning a parcel barcode using their mobile device","how-to-package-books.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6pDc5bqstJ9-cfO_EVRI_LOCATION_04_3711.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6pDc5bqstJ9-cfO",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"feature_banner$37b0ec7e-5830-41a0-aab0-b84c6a054ffe",{"variation":53,"version":26,"items":255,"primary":257,"id":302,"slice_type":79,"slice_label":30},[256],{},{"CardImage":258,"CardAvatar":66,"CardTitle":264,"CardText":265,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":259,"alt":260,"copyright":30,"url":261,"id":262,"edit":263},{"width":59,"height":60},"Customer sat at a desk unpeeling a printed delivery label to place onto the parcel in front of them.","how-to-package-books.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6R6EJbqstJ9-ST7_EVRI_LOCATION_05_8647.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&w=1000&h=667","Z6R6EJbqstJ9-ST7",{"x":45,"y":45,"zoom":46,"background":65},"Ensure you’ve labelled your parcel properly",[266,275,278,281,290,293],{"type":34,"text":267,"spans":268,"direction":163},"Labelling your parcel correctly is very important. Without the right label, your Courier won’t be able to deliver your parcel – and you don’t want the whole packaging process to go to waste after putting in so much time and effort.",[269,274],{"start":45,"end":270,"type":170,"data":271},31,{"link_type":172,"url":272,"target":273},"how-to-package-books.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fguides\u002Fhow-to-label-a-parcel","_blank",{"start":45,"end":270,"type":176},{"type":34,"text":276,"spans":277,"direction":163},"To find the right parcel label, be sure to enter the details of your parcel correctly online. You can then print your label off at home or at one of our ParcelShops before putting it in plain view on your parcel.",[],{"type":34,"text":279,"spans":280,"direction":163},"Once you’ve got you’ve label ready, you can arrange for a courier to collect your parcel, or drop it off at your local ParcelShop or Locker. No matter the package, our team of couriers will get it to its destination on time and in great condition. ",[],{"type":34,"text":282,"spans":283,"direction":163},"For more details on prepping any parcel for delivery, visit our How to send a parcel page.",[284,289],{"start":285,"end":286,"type":170,"data":287},64,89,{"link_type":172,"url":288,"target":273},"how-to-package-books.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fsend\u002Fhow-to-send-a-parcel",{"start":285,"end":286,"type":176},{"type":34,"text":291,"spans":292,"direction":163},"Now you have the information you need to package your books correctly, you’ll be ready the next time you need to parcel them up.",[],{"type":34,"text":294,"spans":295,"direction":163},"So, if y